   "mechanism": "TNFSF13 (APRIL) is a cytokine that stimulates B-cell activation and class-switch recombination. In IgA nephropathy, elevated TNFSF13 activity leads to the overproduction of poorly O-glycosylated IgA1, which deposits in the kidney. Inhibitors of TNFSF13, such as atacicept, are in late-stage clinical trials to reduce pathogenic IgA levels and prevent glomerular damage.",
