   "mechanism": "The pathogenesis of IgA nephropathy is closely tied to mucosal immune responses against intestinal pathogens. CARD9, ITGAX, and DEFA4 are crucial for innate immune sensing and defense in mucosal tissues. Alterations in these host-defense mechanisms disrupt intestinal homeostasis, triggering aberrant mucosal immune responses that generate the pathogenic, poorly O-glycosylated IgA1 underlying the disease.",
